while generating directly in pixels.</p>

<h2 id="imagenet">ImageNet</h2>

<p>At 256×256, Detour-XL/16 reaches <strong>FID-50k 1.43</strong> in 200 epochs; at 512×512, Detour-XL/32 reaches
<strong>1.59</strong> in 160 epochs. Without guidance the same models reach 3.69 and 4.19.</p>

<p>Both runs were continued, and both now reach <strong>1.35</strong>: 256×256 gets <strong>1.35</strong> at epoch 320, and
512×512 gets <strong>1.35</strong> at epoch 280. At 512 most of that came from the guidance <em>window</em> rather than
from the extra epochs — the same setting on [0.05, 0.75] measures 1.46 on two separate
runs, and widening to [0.05, 0.9], the value 256 already used, gives 1.35. Epoch 320 at 512 is worse
than 280, so the longer run is not uniformly better.</p>

<p>Guidance matters, and the two kinds compose. Classifier-free guidance alone plateaus; autoguidance
alone is already better at a much lower Inception score; together they are better than either.</p>

